# Track large binary intermediates with Git LFS.
# Requires: git lfs install  (once per machine)
#           git lfs pull     (after cloning to download the files)
#
# Rule: Git LFS holds only files that can be REGENERATED from the repository
# (see "Regenerating the .rds files" in papers/2024-cancers/README.md).
# GitHub release downloads (source zip / tar.gz) contain only LFS pointer
# files, so anything that cannot be regenerated must be a plain git file.
# Those exceptions are listed below the LFS rules.
*.rds filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.RData filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Irreplaceable inputs (plain git, so every release download contains them):
#   the original HPC bootstrap resamples and fits (the exact inputs of the HPC
#   run were not recorded) and the frozen published values.
papers/2024-cancers/data-derived/list_of_resampled_milton_output.rds -filter -diff -merge binary
papers/2024-cancers/data-derived/miltonoutput.rds -filter -diff -merge binary
papers/2024-cancers/data-derived/param_names.rds -filter -diff -merge binary

# rig project shim package: must be plain git, never LFS
.rvenvlib/** -filter -diff -merge
